a commemoration event is being held in  berlin today to mark five years since  the islamist terror attack on a busy  christmas market the attacker first  hijacked a truck killing the driver he  then drove it into crowds at the bright  side christmas market in central berlin  killing 11 more people another man died  a few weeks ago from injuries sustained  that night bringing the death toll to  13.  the attacker anas amri was a failed  tunisian asylum seeker who was known to  authorities a few days later he was shot  dead by police while on the run in italy  the christmas lights are on and the mood  is festive at the market in berlin's  brighcite plots  at first glance it's hard to see any  trace of the terror attack five years  ago  but market trader max miller will never  forget that day he barely escaped with  his life when a truck plowed onto the  site and destroyed his stand  i was at work and heard a loud noise it  sounded like a dumpster being rolled  away  there was a humming noise in the  background  i turned around and saw the truck and  what happened  then my wife and i ran to safety  13 people were killed in the attack and  more than 60 wounded the horror is not  forgotten  despite this max miller has opened a new  stand at the christmas market  he prefers not to show us because he  doesn't want publicity how did he find  the courage to return to the scene  i would say this is the best way of  dealing with trauma i was in therapy and  learned how to cope with my feelings  but it will be with me for the rest of  my life and when my children ask me  daddy what was it like on that day i  will probably stutter a little before i  can tell them the story  many visitors have mixed feelings about  being at the christmas market there is a  holiday atmosphere  but also a sense of grief  especially at the memorial to the  victims  [Music]  i feel a chill running down my spine i  can't put it into words  when you see the lights and smell the  hot dogs then you can forget the bad  things for a little while  it was horrible that you can't change  what happened  giving in to the terrorists was never an  option says trader max miller and his  colleagues agree  it will always be with us  you can't forget something like that  [Music]  but we all said we have to keep going  and not look back  the memory of the attack will never go  away  but today the christmas spirit has  returned to berlin's brideside plots
 

